/home/koby/.claude/projects/-home-koby/5a62d8bf-3773-4e9a-9d0d-7cb400ed6e73.jsonl:2406:{"parentUuid":"b3263923-e366-490a-ad9e-150d86614e7b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfL2J4yu6RbnZB5xBs6SE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"It's everybody's favorite time, KOBY BOWSER TIME!\n\nHere's the full state of play on the qmail → Postfix migration.\n\n## The setup\n\nThree legacy qmail-ldap sites (`smtp-mtq-1` = 64,492 accounts, `smtp-guy-1` = 121,461, `smtp-gua-1` = 121,455) migrating to a unified Postfix/Dovecot target (`mtq-mailsrvp-01`). Also found a 4th LDAP server (`172.30.37.225`, 121,858 accounts) that turned out to be guy/gua's likely real upstream source — unrelated to mtq. Strategy: domain-by-domain, pilot first.\n\n**Architecture decision:** LDAP stays where it is during the transition — Dovecot queries it remotely via a dedicated read-only service account, rather than migrating/copying the directory. Keeps qmail and Postfix reading the same source of truth, safe rollback if needed.\n\n## Pilot domain: `ool.fr` (12 accounts, mtq)\n\nChosen over `business.ool.fr` (data corruption) and `rife.re` (pure forwards, no real mailboxes). Clean data, `{SHA}`-hashed passwords (no resets needed), login rule validated against the full 64,492-account dataset (`active` or `enabled` status, excluding `forwardonly`).\n\n## Done\n\n- **Phase 3**: `cn=dovecot-auth,ou=services,o=ool` service account created and verified in LDAP on `smtp-mtq-1`.\n- **Phase 4**: auth filter logic and attribute mappings finalized, config file corrected onto the right host (`mtq-mailsrvp-01`) with correct permissions and hostname resolution.\n- Identified and quantified a systemic legacy issue: **59,486 \"sentmail-\\*\" files** across mtq from a 2012–2014 webmail app, needing a real conversion tool before migration.\n- Wrote a full French project write-up, ready for you to paste into Outline (I can't reach `wiki.corp.intranet.local` myself — internal-only host, no route from my sandbox).\n\n## Currently blocked — Phase 5\n\nWiring LDAP into Dovecot's auth stack is stuck on **Dovecot 2.4.1's completely redesigned LDAP config syntax**. We've tried multiple setting-name variants (`args`, `passdb_ldap_args`, `passdb_ldap_filter` nested and top-level, plain `filter=`) — all rejected by `doveconf -n`. Official docs are returning 503s, third-party sources are inconsistent across versions. Current lead, not yet checked: **no LDAP auth module exists on the box, and no `dovecot-ldap`-style package shows in `dpkg -l`** — working theory is a missing package, not a syntax mistake. Next command queued: `apt-cache search dovecot | grep -i ldap`.\n\n## Still open\n\n- `smtp-mtq-1`'s 31,334-message stuck mail queue (uninvestigated).\n- Account dedup across all 4 LDAP sources.\n- Where contacts/address books actually live.\n- guy vs. gua live-traffic determination.\n- LDAP relocation plan before `smtp-mtq-1`'s eventual full shutdown.\n\nWant to run that `apt-cache search` now and get Phase 5 unstuck?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":502346,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1475,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":340},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":502346,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1475,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":502346,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":502346},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"previous_message_not_found"}},"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"6e62f4b4-8728-4633-b125-c9d2283340cc","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"re